        <briefdescription>
<para>Overlays one disk lua file onto the existing tree in place. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Parses the lua file, walks the resulting ValueTree in lockstep with the live state, and mutates properties that differ (see <ref refid="classjam_1_1Model_1a60302bd42d072320d9a918051250b6a6" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::Model::setValuesFrom</ref>). No child add/remove. Listeners stay bound; parameters pick up new values on next flush.</para>
<para>Filename stem (e.g. &quot;display&quot; from &quot;display.lua&quot;) maps to tree section. Parse failures reported via errorOut (<ulink url="file:line">file:line</ulink>) — tree keeps existing values. Caller must have called build() first.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>file</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Lua config file to load. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>errorOut</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Out-param — populated with &quot;file:line: message&quot; on parse failure. Cleared on success. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
